course: dictionary
lesson: 11535
title: Alteration means a change
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An alteration is a change made to something. A tailor makes alterations to clothes, such as shortening trousers so they fit better. «The tailor made a few alterations to my trousers so they fit.» The word tells you that something was changed, and the sentence tells you why.
explain: You can make alterations to many things. «Our builders are making alterations to the kitchen this summer.» They are changing the kitchen, not building a new house. In English lessons, you can make alterations to your writing to improve it: «Please make alterations to your story after you read it again.»
explain: Sometimes a sign says «No alterations allowed.» This is a formal way of saying you must not change the thing. Use the clues: a shop sign about clothes means you cannot change the clothes, and a sign on a test paper would mean you cannot change your answers.
fact: An alteration is a change made to something.
fact: «Alteration» is a noun. The verb is «alter», which means to change.
fact: «Make alterations» is a common phrase, as in «make alterations to your writing».
fact: «Minor alterations» means small changes, not big ones.
fact: A tailor does alterations to clothes, such as shortening trousers or taking in a jacket.
exercise: «The tailor made alterations to the trousers.» What is an alteration? | A new pair of shoes | *A change made to something | A kind of thread | A bag for carrying clothes
exercise: «Our builders are making minor alterations to the kitchen.» What does minor mean here? | Hidden under the floor | *Small | Huge | Painted in bright colours
exercise: A sign in a shop says «No alterations allowed.» What does it mean? | *You must not change the item | The shop is closing early | You get a free gift | You can change the item as you like
test: «She asked the tailor for alterations to her new dress.» What did she want? | Her dress washed and ironed | A different colour dress | A brand new dress from the shop | *Changes so the dress fits her better
test: Which is a good way to make alterations to your writing? | Read it once and never look at it again | Throw the story in the bin | *Cross out a weak sentence and rewrite it to be clearer | Add a title in tiny letters
exam: After you read your story, what might you make to improve it? | *Alterations to make it better | Fog in the classroom | A bigger pencil case | A lot of noise
